  <issue>
  Feature request: Enable use of unix-style line endings when running sqlfluff fix command on Windows
In our environment, we use Windows PCs for development, but the company standard is that SQL files have unix-style line endings (LF).  We use bash under WSL a lot, and set Windows editors to use LF only.  However, the only python we have available is on Windows. When running sqlfluff fix under python on Windows, the file gets changed from LF to Windows-style line endings CRLF.

I understand that this is python default behavior, but it would be nice to be able to over-ride the default and choose LF only, all the time.
  </issue>
  
